d}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot 3564 \\\\  & =297.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =297-{(-15)}^{2} \\\\  & =297-225 \\\\  & =72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247582 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247583 13194139533698 true] [17592186247582 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533698 true] [17592186247582 1041 "field-1" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247582 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247583 13194139533698 true] [17592186247582 1110 #uuid "d9803225-96c4-5426-a1c0-d3e70f19eb16" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247583 1034 "72" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247583 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533698 true] [17592186247583 1111 #uuid "afe6aa64-af78-5b7a-a7e7-4ac14701ea04" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247585 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1089 "q-263585" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1100 "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n15,\\,1,\\,-10,\\,-13,\\,-9\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1113 #uuid "3465a7ef-ecfc-5da2-88a3-b3ddd7544d34" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1138 false 13194139533698 true] [17592186247584 1145 "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=5$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (15+1-10-13-9) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (-16) \\\\  & =-\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [{15}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-10)^{2}+(-13)^{2}+(-9)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot [225+1+100+169+81] \\\\  & =\\frac{576}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{576}{5}-{(-\\frac{16}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{576}{5}-\\frac{256}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2880-256}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2624}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2624}{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{41}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247586 13194139533698 true] [17592186247585 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247587 13194139533698 true] [17592186247585 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533698 true] [17592186247585 1041 "field-1" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247585 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247586 13194139533698 true] [17592186247585 1110 #uuid "93cf3cb4-f063-579d-b843-5746e3f2559c" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247586 1034 "\\frac{8\\sqrt{41}}{5}" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247586 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533698 true] [17592186247586 1111 #uuid "a336db98-e2dc-568a-be6c-cc284ba8b3a3" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247587 1034 "10" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247587 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533698 true] [17592186247587 1111 #uuid "3c15ddad-12e2-50b5-a3d4-99afc6713ffe" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1017 #edb/ref 17592186247589 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1089 "q-263596" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1100 "Compute the standard deviation $\\sigma $ of the following data set:\n\n$$\n-9,\\,-5,\\,3,\\,8,\\,-1,\\,-4,\\,-6\n$$\n\nDo not round your answer.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1113 #uuid "9f2f806f-af5f-57af-8c6f-9650c646c6b1" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1138 false 13194139533698 true] [17592186247588 1145 "The standard deviation of a data set ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is the square root of the variance:\n\n$$\n\\sigma =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2}}=\\sqrt{\\,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-{(\\overset{―}{x})}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=7$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-9-5+3+8-1-4-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-14) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [(-9)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-6)^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot [81+25+9+64+1+16+36] \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}-{(-2)}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{232}{7}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{232-28}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{204}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the standard deviation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sigma  & =\\sqrt{{\\sigma }^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{204}{7}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{\\frac{51}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247589 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247590 13194139533698 true] [17592186247589 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533698 true] [17592186247589 1041 "field-1" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247589 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247590 13194139533698 true] [17592186247589 1110 #uuid "817592ad-1532-5690-8cb1-8201f69d28d6" 131941