6247598 1138 false 13194139533698 true] [17592186247598 1145 "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the variance can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\sigma }^{2}=\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\overset{―}{x}$ is the mean of the data set and $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}$ is the mean of the squares of the points in the data set.\n\nFirst, let's compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ There are $n=9$ points in our data set, so the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (1+5+1+2+3+6+1+2+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}.$ Computing the mean of the squares of the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot ({1}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot (1+25+1+4+9+36+1+4+36) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\cdot 117 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\overset{―}{{x}^{2}}-(\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =13-{(3)}^{2} \\\\  & =13-9 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247600 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247601 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247602 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247603 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247604 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1041 "selection" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247604 13194139533698 true] [17592186247599 1110 #uuid "0ce7a91f-7cad-5def-b2a5-200f3d55d4c0" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247600 1034 "9" 13194139533698 true] [17592186247600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139